   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <p>Dear Léon: A few scribbled lines to catch post. Has <unclear reason="illegible">Miss</unclear> M. sent U to <name type="person" key="loyrXX">Loy</name>? <name type="person" key="budg82">Budgen</name> should know that his publishers never sent <name type="work">his book</name> either to <name type="person" key="fehr76">prof. Fehr</name> or to the <hi rend="underline">N</hi>.<hi rend="underline">Z</hi>.<hi rend="underline">Z</hi>.. Also <name type="person" key="verh00">
                            <choice>
                                <sic>ver Hulst</sic>
                                <corr>Verhulst</corr>
                            </choice>
                        </name> should send the <hi rend="underline">Mime</hi> to him. <name type="person" key="jola94">Jolas</name> leaves tomorrow. I enclose U.S. letter. Am not sending <name type="person" key="joyc07">Lucia</name>’s letters after all. What a problem! Hope to see Dr. <unclear reason="illegible">Stirling</unclear> tomorrow. Hope you are well.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <salute>        	<foreign xml:lang="fra">cordialement votre</foreign>
                        </salute>
                        <signed>                    	<name type="person" key="joyc82">James Joyce</name>
                        </signed>
                        <dateline>
                            <date when="1934-10-14">14.10.’34</date>
                        </dateline>
                    </closer>
                </div>
            </div>
      </body>
   </text>
